// URI references, RFC 3986:
// https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc3986
//
// Taking one apart, putting one back together, resolving a relative one against
// a base, and the percent coding that lets any octet travel inside one. This is
// the addressing syntax every other package here spells out in full and nobody
// owns — a form body, a request target, a `Location` header and a data URL all
// obey it.
//
// Percent coding takes the component as a parameter rather than a hand-written
// list of spared characters: which octets may stand for themselves is decided by
// RFC 3986's grammar, and three callers writing that list out by hand is three
// chances to get it wrong.
//
// Not here: internationalised host names (RFC 3492), and the parts of the WHATWG
// URL Standard that are specific to it rather than to RFC 3986 — special
// schemes, default ports, Windows drive letters.
import {
  "moonbitlang/core/encoding/utf8",
}

import {
  "moonbitstack/moonhttp/url",
} for "test"
